# Language parity

C# is the reference language. When public APIs or runtime behavior diverge, change Rust and TypeScript to match C#. Do not add a helper, extra call, or auto-path in one language only.

`Defaults` / `Create` / `Register` / `Default` mean the same thing everywhere. If env already has `INSTALLED_PROVIDERS` and `DATASOURCE_URL`, `Default` / `default` / `DatasourceFactory.default` applies those defaults and registers the listed factories. Do not require `install`, `register_from`, or a hand-built defaults dictionary in one language when the others do not.

```csharp
var ds = DatasourceFactory.Default;
```

```rust
let ds = default()?;
```

```typescript
const ds = DatasourceFactory.default;
```
